## 1. `lib/db/src/index.ts` — barrel export pattern

`/home/runner/workspace/lib/db/src/index.ts:22` does `export * from "./schema";`, and `/home/runner/workspace/lib/db/src/schema/index.ts` is a flat re-export list:

```ts
export * from "./shows";
export * from "./tasks";
export * from "./eblasts";
export * from "./links";
export * from "./officeTasks";
export * from "./venues";
export * from "./presetTasks";
export * from "./gcalOrphans";
```

`gcalOrphansTable` itself is defined in `/home/runner/workspace/lib/db/src/schema/gcalOrphans.ts`:

```ts
import { pgTable, text, serial, timestamp } from "drizzle-orm/pg-core";

export const gcalOrphansTable = pgTable("gcal_orphans", {
  id: serial("id").primaryKey(),
  gcalEventId: text("gcal_event_id").notNull(),
  calendarType: text("calendar_type").notNull().default("task"),
  createdAt: timestamp("created_at", { withTimezone: true }).notNull().defaultNow(),
});
```

For a new `todoistOrphansTable`, the pattern is: create `lib/db/src/schema/todoistOrphans.ts` defining/exporting the table, then add `export * from "./todoistOrphans";` to `lib/db/src/schema/index.ts`. No changes needed to `lib/db/src/index.ts` itself since it already does `export * from "./schema"`. It'll then be importable as `import { todoistOrphansTable } from "@workspace/db"` exactly like `gcalOrphansTable`.

## 2. Orphan-insert logic in delete handlers

**`artifacts/api-server/src/routes/tasks.ts:129-158`** — `DELETE /:taskId`:
```ts
router.delete("/:taskId", async (req, res): Promise<void> => {
  const params = DeleteTaskParams.safeParse({ showId: Number(req.params.showId), taskId: Number(req.params.taskId) });
  if (!params.success) { res.status(400).json({ error: "Invalid params" }); return; }

  const [task] = await db
    .select({ gcalEventId: tasksTable.gcalEventId })
    .from(tasksTable)
    .where(and(eq(tasksTable.id, params.data.taskId), eq(tasksTable.showId, params.data.showId)));

  if (task?.gcalEventId) {
    await db.insert(gcalOrphansTable).values({ gcalEventId: task.gcalEventId, calendarType: "task" });
  }

  await db.delete(tasksTable).where(and(eq(tasksTable.id, params.data.taskId), eq(tasksTable.showId, params.data.showId)));
  res.status(204).send();
});
```
Gate condition: only inserts an orphan row if the task row being deleted has a non-null `gcalEventId` (i.e., it was previously synced). `calendarType` is hardcoded to `"task"`.

**`artifacts/api-server/src/routes/eblasts.ts:128-157`** — identical shape, `DELETE /:eblastId`, gated on `eblast?.gcalEventId`, inserts with `calendarType: "eblast"`.

**`artifacts/api-server/src/routes/shows.ts:218-243`** — cascade delete of a show:
```ts
router.delete("/:showId", async (req, res): Promise<void> => {
  const params = DeleteShowParams.safeParse({ showId: Number(req.params.showId) });
  if (!params.success) { res.status(400).json({ error: "Invalid show ID" }); return; }

  const [childTasks, childEblasts] = await Promise.all([
    db.select({ gcalEventId: tasksTable.gcalEventId }).from(tasksTable).where(eq(tasksTable.showId, params.data.showId)),
    db.select({ gcalEventId: eblastsTable.gcalEventId }).from(eblastsTable).where(eq(eblastsTable.showId, params.data.showId)),
  ]);

  const taskOrphanIds = childTasks.map((t) => t.gcalEventId).filter((id): id is string => !!id);
  const eblastOrphanIds = childEblasts.map((e) => e.gcalEventId).filter((id): id is string => !!id);
  const allOrphans = [
    ...taskOrphanIds.map((gcalEventId) => ({ gcalEventId, calendarType: "task" as const })),
    ...eblastOrphanIds.map((gcalEventId) => ({ gcalEventId, calendarType: "eblast" as const })),
  ];

  if (allOrphans.length > 0) {
    await db.insert(gcalOrphansTable).values(allOrphans);
  }

  await db.delete(showsTable).where(eq(showsTable.id, params.data.showId));
  res.status(204).send();
});
```
Batch-selects `gcalEventId` from both child tasks and eblasts for the show, filters out nulls, tags each with the appropriate `calendarType`, and bulk-inserts in one `db.insert(...).values(array)` call before deleting the show row (cascade relies on DB FK cascade or is otherwise not shown here — tasks/eblasts rows themselves aren't explicitly deleted in this snippet, presumably FK `ON DELETE CASCADE`).

## 3. Generated hook naming/calling convention (`lib/api-client-react/src/generated/api.ts`)

Pattern confirmed for `listGoogleCalendars` (query, `:2636-2702`) and `syncGoogleCalendar` (mutation, `:2704-2798`). OpenAPI orval-style codegen produces, per operationId `xxx`:
- `xxxUrl` — URL builder (query params via `URLSearchParams` if the op has params)
- `xxx` (async fn) — raw fetch wrapper using `customFetch`
- `getXxxQueryKey` / `getXxxQueryOptions` (queries) or `getXxxMutationOptions` (mutations)
- `useXxx` — the exported hook, i.e. `useListGoogleCalendars`, `useSyncGoogleCalendar`

So `listTodoistProjects` → `useListTodoistProjects`, `syncTodoist` → `useSyncTodoist`, following exact camelCase-with-`use`-prefix.

Calling convention (query hooks with params), confirmed via actual usage in `/home/runner/workspace/artifacts/show-command-center/src/components/dashboard-weekly-calendar.tsx:57-64`:
```ts
const { data: events1 } = useGetCalendarEvents(
  { month: startMonth, year: startYear },
  { query: { queryKey: ["weekly-cal", startMonth, startYear] } }
);
```
i.e. `useXxx(paramsObject, { query: { ...UseQueryOptions overrides } })` for queries. For mutations (`useSyncGoogleCalendar` shape, `:2780-2798`), the hook takes `{ mutation?: UseMutationOptions..., request?: ... }` and the mutate function is called with `{ params?: SyncGoogleCalendarParams }` as its variables argument (i.e. `mutate({ params: { calendarId: "..." } })`), not the params directly as a positional arg — that's the query-vs-mutation asymmetry to watch for when wiring up `useSyncTodoist`.

Barrel: `/home/runner/workspace/lib/api-client-react/src/index.ts` re-exports `./generated/api` and `./generated/api.schemas`, so hooks are imported from `@workspace/api-client-react` (confirmed via `import { useGetCalendarEvents } from "@workspace/api-client-react";` in the same file).

